 "format": "Commander",
 "name": "Captain America: Shield Throw",
 "notes": [
  "Plan: Cap is a 4/4 for three. At the start of each combat he attaches one Equipment you control for free (Catch). For {3} he unattaches one and deals damage equal to its mana value, split among up to three targets (Throw). Next combat he catches it again.",
  "Best catches: Colossus Hammer (+10/+10 with no equip cost), Argentum Armor (destroys a permanent each attack, then throws for 6), Swordsman's Steel, Hulkbuster Armor and Hammer of Nazahn (throw for 4 each).",
  "Catch targets the Equipment, not Cap, so it still works while he wears Lightning Greaves.",
  "Card flow: The Mighty Thor, Sram and Puresteel Paladin draw as Equipment arrives; Rogue's Gloves, Mask of Memory, Akiri, Wyleth and Tome of Legends draw as he attacks.",
  "Mjölnir, Storm Hammer is the single copy from the History of Heroes kit. Black Panther was its other candidate home; it is listed here for now.",
  "Ownership tags on each card: have = confirmed owned; freed = from a deck folded Nov 16 or a precon cut; likely = Marvel common or uncommon, or your staples pile; check = owned but maybe sleeved elsewhere; buy = not known to be owned.",
  "Buy list (Nov 12 snapshot): about $6.50 for the six buy cards, plus the commander. Estimated, not simulated: commander-damage kills around turns 7-9.",
  "Bracket 2 check: 0 Game Changers, no extra turns, no land destruction, no two-card infinite. One tutor (Open the Armory) plus Captain America, Liberator and Sun-Spider."
 ],
